<title>ESTONIA: TALIBOR/TALIBID INTERBANK 1-MO RATES RISE.</title>
<headline>TALIBOR/TALIBID INTERBANK 1-MO RATES RISE.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average interbank rates rose in</p>
<p>the one-month period while one-week and three-month rates</p>
<p>stable, the central bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The increase was surprising, as liquidity has been very</p>
<p>good and the number of transactions has been very low,&quot; Erki</p>
<p>Raasuke, head of Hansapank's money market desk, told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;Someone, for whatever reason, has adjusted their rates and</p>
<p>this is reflected in the change,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Raasuke said that the good liquidity is expected to stay and</p>
<p>no significant changes are expected during the next week.</p>
<p>    TALIBOR/TALIBID   1Week	 1Month    3Month</p>
<p>    August 6	    4.25/3.25  5.62/4.62  7.00/6.00</p>
<p>    July 30	     4.25/3.25  5.52/4.52  7.00/6.00</p>
<p>-- Tallinn newsroom +372 620 9202 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
